# Questions & Answers

---

## 1. Tell me about your daily routine.

### 💡 Ideas

- Wake up early
- Exercise
- Study or work
- Read
- Sleep on time

### 🗣️ Sample Answer

My daily routine is quite structured because I like to stay organised. I usually wake up around 6:30 a.m., freshen up, and spend some time exercising or reviewing my study plan. During the day, I focus on work or studying, and in the evening I revise English, read a book, or spend time with my family. Before going to bed, I usually plan my tasks for the following day.

---

## 2. Has your daily routine changed since you were a child?

### 💡 Ideas

- Yes
- School
- Now work
- More responsibilities

### 🗣️ Sample Answer

Yes, it has changed significantly. When I was a child, my routine mainly revolved around school, homework, and playing with friends. Nowadays, I have many more responsibilities, so I spend most of my time working, learning new skills, and planning for my future.

---

## 3. Is your daily routine different at the weekend from during the week?

### 💡 Ideas

- Yes
- Relax
- Family
- Less work

### 🗣️ Sample Answer

Yes, there's quite a noticeable difference. During the week, I usually follow a strict schedule because of work or study commitments. At weekends, however, I allow myself to relax a bit more, spend quality time with my family, watch films, or go out with friends.

---

## 4. What would you like to change about your daily routine?

### 💡 Ideas

- Exercise more
- Sleep earlier
- Read more books

### 🗣️ Sample Answer

If I could change one thing, I'd like to dedicate more time to exercise and reading. Sometimes I become so busy with work and studying that I don't maintain a healthy balance. I believe improving these habits would make me more productive and healthier in the long run.

---

## 5. Do you think it's important to have a daily routine?

### 💡 Ideas

- Yes
- Discipline
- Productivity
- Less stress

### 🗣️ Sample Answer

Absolutely. Having a daily routine helps people manage their time effectively and stay productive. It also reduces stress because you know exactly what needs to be done. In my opinion, a well-planned routine is one of the keys to achieving long-term goals.

